    <string name="login_security_notice_title">Security Notice</string>
    <string name="login_security_notice_1">    The password is encrypted on-device via AES-CBC and sent directly to the school CAS unified authentication server. Encryption uses a dynamic salt issued by the school login page, unique for each request. This app never sends passwords to any third-party server.</string>
    <string name="login_security_notice_2">    After successful login, only cookies are stored locally on the device, persisted via the Android system WebKit CookieManager, accessible only by this app. The \"remember password\" feature encrypts and stores credentials in the device\'s private storage, enabled only when the user chooses.</string>
    <string name="login_security_notice_3">    Each user\'s login session is stored independently and does not interfere with others. Local login data can be deleted at any time from the login screen.</string>
    <string name="login_security_notice_4">    QR login and adding accounts use independent cookie environments and do not carry any existing user session information.</string>
    <string name="login_security_notice_5">    Exporting login credentials requires device password verification. Exported data is AES-encrypted with custom password protection, and importing requires the same decryption password, ensuring safe credential migration between devices.</string>
